# CREDENTIALS & CONFIG (NEVER PUSH KEYS)
config.json
.env

# GOOGLE OAUTH. secrets/ holds the downloaded client file and the token the loopback
# flow exchanges for it - an access token, a refresh token and the account's address.
# A refresh token does not expire on its own, which makes this folder strictly worse to
# leak than config.json, and config.json is already in this repo's history. The folder is
# listed before it exists on purpose: the ignore rule is the cheap half and the rotation
# is the expensive one. The server never serves anything outside viewer/, so nothing in
# here is reachable from the browser either.
secrets/

# THE DOORMAN'S MEMORY. speaker-store/ holds one json per enrolled voice, and each one
# carries 192 floats that are a measurement of a person's larynx. No audio is in there -
# nothing in voiceprint.py can write a sample - so it cannot be played back, but an
# embedding is still biometric data about a named human being and it does not belong in a
# repository any more than a refresh token does. Listed beside secrets/ for that reason and
# denied to Read in .claude/settings.json for the same one. The server never serves
# anything outside viewer/, so it is not reachable from the browser either.
speaker-store/

# THE DOWNLOADED WEIGHTS. models/ is the ECAPA-TDNN ONNX file the doorman embeds with:
# 24.9 MB of somebody else's published weights, fetched once, an asset rather than source
# and rebuildable by re-downloading it. Same reason voices/ is ignored. README says which
# file and where.
models/

# PYTHON CACHES
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
.venv/
venv/

# LOGS & OUTPUTS
*.log
*.out
server.log
live.out
pf.out
server.out

# GENERATED LOCAL STATE
notes-index.json
# THE VECTOR STORE. Derived data, every byte of it: a sqlite file, an HNSW index and a
# manifest of hashes, all rebuildable from notes/ and archive/ with one command. It is
# also large, binary and rewritten on every build, which is three separate reasons a
# version control system should never see it. "python build.py" is the source.
vector-store/
focus-ledger.json
tools-ledger.json
calendar.json

# PROOF ARTEFACTS (screenshots the harnesses write)
deck-*.png

# ROUND ARTEFACTS. _runs/ is every harness summary as it was printed and _spoken/ is the
# recorded room audio behind the spoken column of the fixture table - evidence for
# console_lookbook.md rather than source, regenerated by re-running the harnesses, and in
# _spoken/'s case a recording of a real microphone in a real room.
_runs/
_spoken/

# THE LOCAL VOICE. A piper model is ~116 MB of weights that belong to whoever
# published them, and say-cache/ is generated audio - both are downloads and neither
# is source. README says which model to fetch and where to put it.
voices/
say-cache/

# OS & IDE FILES
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.vscode/
.idea/